## Discipline self-audit

- [ ] Test set sealed until Phase 5; opened ONCE
- [ ] Pre-registered metric + threshold; no drift
- [ ] Pilot N=1 validated all metric fields populated before full dev run
- [ ] Distribution audit: per-slice counts match production traffic shape
- [ ] Variance baseline measured (>=3 same-prompt trials)
- [ ] Effect >= 2× variance, not just >= threshold
- [ ] Cross-judge sanity check on >=5 rows with a 2nd-family judge
- [ ] Blind judge (arm labels anonymized per row)
- [ ] Each iter changed ONE thing in the arm
- [ ] Iter hypotheses written in advance; falsification accepted as finished
- [ ] 3-iteration cap enforced
- [ ] Verdict locks LATEST hypothesis-driven iter, not best-scoring iter
- [ ] Per-slice scores reported; aggregate winners hold on all major slices, OR ship is scoped narrowly
- [ ] Failure-mode categories pre-registered in Phase 2; per-category delta reported above
- [ ] If severity weighting used: both unweighted + weighted aggregates reported; disagreements surfaced in verdict

